    "body": "## Summary\n- add Flyway V17 with a hierarchical job/service category catalog and initial production-oriented seed set\n- model leaf fulfillment semantics explicitly as `ON_SITE` or `POINT_TO_POINT`\n- expose public `GET /job-categories` returning an ordered hierarchy suitable for the create-job UI\n- add persistence mapping/repository and deterministic hierarchy projection\n- permit anonymous category discovery without weakening authenticated job mutations\n- cover hierarchy ordering and fulfillment-mode projection with a focused unit test\n\n## Seeded areas\nTransport/przeprowadzki, paczki/kurier, zakupy i dostawy, dom/remont, sprzątanie, ogród, zwierzęta, technologia, sprawy codzienne, utylizacja i pomoc przy pojazdach, with leaf subcategories including restaurant pickup, store shopping, furniture/AGD transport, moving, handyman, plumbing/electrical and others.\n\n## Follow-up boundary\nThis PR deliberately establishes the catalog/API first. The next atomic step will require a selectable leaf category on job creation and enforce fulfillment-specific location rules (`ON_SITE` vs `POINT_TO_POINT`) without coupling that larger request/route refactor to the catalog migration.\n\n## Validation\nBranch is directly based on current master including the PostgreSQL null-query regression fix. CI is the merge gate; do not merge unless backend tests/build and runtime/Flyway smoke checks pass.",
